# Delete - EdgeQL | Reference
created: undefined, last updated: 2026-06-11, [Read more](https://docs.geldata.com/reference/edgeql/delete)

Every link is associated with a *link deletion policy*.
By default, it isn't possible to delete an object linked to by another.
...
To avoid this behavior, we could update the `Movie.characters` link to use
the `allow` deletion policy.
Copy
```
type Movie {
required title: str { constraint exclusive };
required release_year: int64;
multi characters: Person;
multi characters: Person {
on target delete allow;
};
}
```
### Cascading deletes ​
If a link uses the `delete source` policy, then deleting a *target* of the link will also delete the object that links to it (the *source*).
This behavior can be used to implement cascading deletes; be careful with this power!

